Jahshaka ogre-patch 0063 — the microcode cache holds a shader whose root
layout was discovered by reflection

WHY
    With Photon's VCT cascade chain on (PHOTON-E2), every launch after the
    first two compiled exactly three shaders and no others:

        20LightVctBounceInject_cs
        33LightVctBounceInject_cs
        44LightVctBounceInject_cs

    They are the 4-, 3- and 2-cascade permutations of the VCT bounce-injection
    compute job. The 1-cascade one (13LightVctBounceInject_cs) came out of the
    cache every time, and that difference is the whole diagnosis:

        Samples/Media/VCT/LightVctBounceInject_cs.glsl:13
            @psub( uses_array_bindings, hlms_num_vct_cascades, 1 )

    so every permutation above one cascade sets `uses_array_bindings`,
    HlmsCompute::compileShader (OgreHlmsCompute.cpp:320-321) answers it with
    setAutoReflectArrayBindingsInRootLayout( true ), and VulkanProgram then
    skips the microcode cache on BOTH ends:

        OgreVulkanProgram.cpp:325   read  if( mCustomRootLayout && !mReflectArrayRootLayouts )
        OgreVulkanProgram.cpp:751   write // TODO: Support caching SPIR-Vs with
                                         // mReflectArrayRootLayouts == true ...

    The reason upstream left it as a TODO is real: such a shader is compiled
    TWICE on a cold run — once to find out where its arrays are, and again
    against the root layout those arrays imply — and the second compile's
    preamble (and therefore the microcode key, which is source + preamble)
    depends on what the first compile discovered. An entry stored under that
    key could never be found by a launch that has not compiled anything yet.

WHAT
    * RootLayout gains a const accessor for its array bindings, re-exported
      by VulkanRootLayout (which inherits RootLayout protected).
    * VulkanProgram captures the microcode key in loadFromSource(), BEFORE any
      compile — the key a later launch can compute — and stores under that one.
    * The microcode blob is framed: a magic, the array bindings the reflection
      found, then the SPIR-V. On a hit the bindings are put back into the root
      layout (mRootLayout is re-derived through VulkanGpuProgramManager exactly
      as gatherArrayedDescs would have derived it) and nothing is compiled.
    * The frame is length-checked. A blob from an unpatched build, or a
      truncated one, is rejected and the shader is compiled — this is also the
      only bounds check between that file and vkCreateShaderModule.
    * In OGRE_DEBUG_MODE >= MEDIUM the existing gatherArrayedDescs( true ) on
      the cache-hit path now validates the restored layout against the cached
      SPIR-V on every hit, so a wrong restore is loud rather than silent.

    The second half of upstream's TODO (mCustomRootLayout == false, i.e. a root
    layout written in the shader's own source) is deliberately NOT taken: that
    layout is not known at the point the key has to be built.

COST
    SOURCE patch — every tree re-runs build-ogre.sh. The blob format changes,
    so every existing shader cache is one generation stale; Jahshaka's cache
    fingerprint carries JAHSHAKA_OGRE_PATCH_SERIES, so it is discarded and
    rebuilt automatically on the first launch after the patch.

    No overlap: no other patch in the stack touches these four files.

Verified with `git apply --check` against the pristine pin and
`git apply --reverse --check` after applying.
